//! # Base gameplay - `d_basesNP` (REL module 2)
//!
//! **Synthetic-base warning.** Every address in this module is a *static
//! analysis address* produced by `tools/rel2elf.mjs` with the canonical base
//! **`0x80600000`**. These are **not** runtime addresses: the Wii REL loader
//! chooses the real load address. The REL entry point in this image is
//! `0x806000F0`. Cross-module pointers (`0x8037xxxx`, `0x8042xxxx`) are
//! `main.dol` addresses imported by the REL and keep their absolute values.
//!
//! ## What this module covers
//!
//! `d_basesNP` is the largest NSMBW REL (text `0x806000F0..0x807C60F4`, about
//! 1.86 MB; see `docs/REL.md`). It contains the base-object state registry, the
//! character-change player-select screens, and many reusable stage actors. This
//! file is a semantic slice, not the whole module: 5607 functions across the
//! recorded passes.
//! The wave-2 pass translated 30 functions chosen for explicit class/state
//! names in their strings or for a self-contained call cluster; the wave-3
//! pass added 25 more from the deferred select-screen tails, the
//! `0x806511D0..0x80651910` state/collision helpers, four class-state
//! registration tables, and the registered actor destructor. Wave 4 adds 28
//! functions from four complete stage-actor clusters: `daCannonPipe_c`,
//! `da2DPlayer_c`, `daPowBlock_c`, and `daPropBlock_c`. Wave 5 adds 30
//! functions: the `dNumberOfPeopleChange_c` and `dSelectPlayer_c` select
//! screens, the six-state `daYoshiEgg_c` actor, and the single-state
//! `daShipGear_c` actor. Wave 7 adds 30 functions: the state table, state
//! destructor and constructor of ten water/rotating-pipe/prop actors
//! (`daWaterBubbleCannon_c`, `daWaterMove_c`, `daWireMove_c`,
//! `daWaterAllRail_c`, `daWaterXinfinitMove_c`, `daRotDokan_c`,
//! `daRotDokanCannon_c`, `daElasticKinoko_c`, `daStrongBox_c`, and
//! `daPeachCastleBlock_c`). Wave 9 adds 24 functions: complete state-table,
//! destructor and constructor triples for `daLiftSpinRotationSync_c`,
//! `daLiftWaterWheel_c`, `daPeachCastleSequenceMgrObj_c`, `daHouseLight_c`,
//! `daStand_c`, `daTorchiLight_c`, `daWireCircle_c`, and
//! `daWmYoganPillar_c`. Wave 10 adds 29 functions: the state tables and
//! destructors of three Koopa boss props, `daFireBlitz_c`,
//! `daLiftObjbgVMove_c`, `daLiftScalesStep_c`, `daLiftZenShiroYogan_c`,
//! `daLineTrain_c`, `daMiniGameGunBatteryMgrObj_c` and
//! `daWmSandPillar_c`, plus four actor constructors and four mini-game/model
//! initialisers. Wave 11 adds 30 functions: the
//! `daCastleKokoopaDemo1st_c`, `daCastleLemmyBall_c`, `daJrClownC_c`,
//! `dCollectionCoin_c` and `daMiniGameWireMeshMgrObj_c` state tables, their
//! destructors and state-object helpers, plus three constructors and the
//! constant handler getters. Wave 12 adds 30 functions: the
//! `dCourseClear_c`, `dCourseTimeUp_c`, `dDateFile_c`, `dDemoMessage_c`,
//! `dDrawGame_c`, `dEasyPairing_c`, `dGameOver_c` and `dMessageWindow_c` state
//! tables with their destructors and in-place constructors, the two
//! `dCourseTimeUp_c` array-element helpers, and the
//! `daCastleLemmyThrowBall_c` table, destructor, handler getter and
//! constructor. Wave 13 adds 30 functions: the `dModelPlayDate_c`,
//! `dMultiCourseSelectContents_c`, `dPointResultDateFileFree_c`,
//! `dStaffCreditScore_c`, `dStockItem_c`, `dTheEnd_c`, `dTimeUp_c`,
//! `dScMulti_c`, `dScResult_c` and `dScGameOver_c` state tables, their
//! destructors, the available in-place constructors, and the `dStockItem_c`
//! layout loader. Wave 14 adds 30 functions: complete state-table, destructor
//! and in-place constructor triples for the `dContinue_c`,
//! `dCourseSelectMenu_c`, `dEventOpeningTitle_c`, `dLetterWindow_c`,
//! `dMiniGameCannon_c`, `dModeSelect_c`, `dModelPlayArrow_c`,
//! `dModelPlayBase_c`, `dOtehonClear_c` and `dPointResultDateFile_c` screens.
//! Wave 15 adds 29 functions: the remaining menu and scene state tables
//! (`dCharacterChangeSelectArrow_c`, `dCharacterChangeSelectBase_c`,
//! `dCharacterChangeSelectContents_c`, `dFileSelect_c`, `dMiniGameWire_c`,
//! `dModelPlayManager_c`, `dMultiCourseSelect_c`, `dPointResultMulti_c`,
//! `dOtasukeInfo_c`, `dScWorld9DeMo_c`, `dScCrsin_c`), their registered
//! destructors and the available in-place constructors. Wave 16 adds 30
//! functions: the last two state tables (`dScGameSetup_c` and
//! `dCourseSelectManager_c`), their destructors, the `characterChangeIndicator`
//! helpers, and the remaining untranslated in-place constructors and their
//! allocator wrappers. Wave 17 adds 30 functions: thirteen remaining in-place
//! constructors, eight descriptor-less class registrations, and nine actor
//! model loaders. The class identity of those constructors and registrations
//! is still `// unknown:`; their bodies and every resource string are explicit.
