// 1. `manjirou`, the four-wheel lift the players ride. Its constructor
//    `0x806EFEF0`, model loader [`fn_806f03e0`] and transform writer
//    [`fn_806f0c10`] were recorded earlier. The bodies below are the rest of the
//    class: two `0x5C`-byte motion records at `+0x610`, four wheel-distance
//    accumulators at `+0x718`, a 256-entry angle history at `+0x752`, the
//    per-frame position deltas at `+0x700..+0x714`, and the state word `+0x360`.
// 2. An unnamed respawn spawner: `+0x398` counts 16-byte records at `+0x39C`,
//    each `[x, y, z, flags]`; the per-frame driver re-arms `+0x394` and spawns
//    actor id `0x20F` at every record.
// 3. Small menu/object helpers: a `0x768`-byte screen constructed by
//    [`fn_806f52b0`], a `0x398`-byte object that registers a global manager at
//    `0x8082ED60`, and two record writers.
//
// The float constants cited below were checked against the raw
// `work/rels/elf/d_basesNP.elf` word, not just the decompiler's decimal print.

/// Calls a target that takes one `f32` and returns the integer in `r3`.
///
/// # Original
/// Host-side ABI wrapper for `0x802DCC4C`, which the exports call as
/// `func_0x802dcc4c((double)(float)...)` and store straight into an `int`
/// (`work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/806f1170_FUN_806f1170.c`). The PowerPC
/// call passes the value in `f1`, so an `f32` parameter is correct; Ghidra
/// prints `double` only because the callee has no prototype.
///
/// # Safety
/// `addr` must point to a function with this ABI.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - mechanical wrapper.
#[inline]
unsafe fn call_f32_i32(addr: usize, a: f32) -> i32 {
    let function: extern "C" fn(f32) -> i32 = core::mem::transmute(addr);
    function(a)
}

