/// Points both motion records at the current wheel contact pairs.
///
/// Each record gets two 2-float points: the front record uses `+0x708`/`+0x70C`
/// as its anchor and `+0x710`/`+0x714` as its target, the rear record uses
/// `+0x700`/`+0x704` and `+0x708`/`+0x70C`. Both are handed to `0x800DB590`
/// (unknown: two-point solver) and the record's virtual `+0xC` is then called.
///
/// # Original
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_806f0d00` at `0x806F0D00` (176 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/806f0d00_FUN_806f0d00.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `actor`: live `manjirou` object; deltas `+0x700..+0x714`, records
///   `+0x610`/`+0x66C`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Calls `0x800DB590` twice and virtual slot `+0xC` of both records.
///
/// # Safety
/// `actor` must be live and both records must have a valid vtable.
