/// After the shared state query, the callback tests the record's kind byte at
/// `+0x38C`. For kind `1` it compares the frame value `0x808063B0` with the
/// constant `0x807CCA7C` (0.0) and either reports id `5` (record crossing the
/// value, `phase == 0`) or id `6` (`phase == 1`).
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80710290` at `0x80710290` (292 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/80710290_FUN_80710290.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `actor` - owner of the range object created at `+0x5B0`.
/// * `event` - callback record; halfword `+0x08` is the event id, byte `+0x38C`
///   the kind (`1` = player-like).
/// * `phase` - callback phase word; the C tests it for `0` and `1`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// The shared interface queries, an optional state switch, and one call to
/// `0x80056370(record, actor, 5|6)`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `actor`, `event` and both vtables must be live.
