///
/// The owner is the incoming `r3`. For each of the four `0x60`-byte records at
/// `+0x504` the attached list at `+0x10` is walked through its `+0x0C` links. An
/// attached object with kind byte `+0x38C == 1` contributes its character index
/// (byte returned by class virtual `+0x6C`) and, through `0x8012DBE0`, its
/// rider's index; kind `2` contributes its own index only. The mask is the
/// routine's `r3` return.
