/// Builds the 9x12 unlock table and copies the saved row order into both
/// layouts.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80607740` at `0x80607740` (504 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/80607740_FUN_80607740.c`
/// - Removed: the modelled `_savegpr_21` prologue call (`0x802DCD5C`) and the
///   `_restgpr_21` epilogue call (`0x802DCDA8`). The prologue `bl` returns no
///   value; `mr r31,r3` right after it is the screen, so `r3` is the incoming
///   argument rather than a getter result.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `screen`: the coin-date screen, incoming `r3`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// For each of nine players and twelve characters it writes the player index
/// (`+0x47C`), the character id (`+0x480`) and either `-1` or a three-bit
/// unlock mask (`+0x484`) from `0x800CE210`. It then copies the twenty-four
/// saved words at `+0x7C` into the two layouts at `+0x74`/`+0x78` as twelve
/// words each, and queues `0x80823070`.
