/// eight-step halfword table at `0x807CD6F0` (written to `+0x9D4`), bit 3
/// selects `0x8000` or `0` for the pitch word `+0x104`, bit 4 selects the armed
/// record count (`+0x9EC` becomes `1` or `3`), bit 8 is copied to the direction
/// byte `+0x348`, and bits 12..15 are copied to `+0xA06`. The four `0xE4`-byte
/// arm records at `+0x5BC` are then bound through `0x8007FB10`, with the
/// callback `0x807316F0` and the `+0x688` frame budget installed only on the
/// record selected by `+0x9EC`.
