/// Initialises a two-axis emitter pair and starts a ten-argument effect.
///
/// `f31 = *(f32*)(this+0x474) * 0.5`, `f30 = *(f32*)(this+0x478) * 0.5`.
/// `0x8008C3E0(this+0x148, this, &0.0)` primes the sub-object, the four floats
/// `+0x164..+0x170` are written as `(0.0, f30, f31, 1.0 + f30)`, the sub-object
/// is finalised, and `0x807242C0(this)` runs. The builder `0x8007FA40` then
/// receives `(this+0x4CC, this, -f31, *(f32*)(this+0x478), f31, 0.0, cb1, cb2,
/// cb3, 1, 0, 0)`. Finally `+0x5AA = +0x38F`, `+0x59C = 0x940`, and
/// `0x8007F900(this+0x4CC)` starts the effect.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_807241c0` at `0x807241C0` (256 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/807241c0_FUN_807241c0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - actor: extents `+0x474`/`+0x478`, emitter `+0x4CC`, sub-object
///   `+0x148`.
