/// Returns the residual height error at a 16-unit quantised sample.
///
/// Reads the global timer object's heights `+0x3C` and `+0x44`, computes
/// `+0x3C - 16`, quantises the absolute sample offset to a 16-unit step, asks
/// [`fn_806561b0`] for a correction count, and returns `error - 16 * count`.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80656260` at `0x80656260` (172 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/80656260_FUN_80656260.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - actor forwarded untouched as the first argument of the call.
///
