/// Decrements a per-entry timer and advances one of four frame slots when it runs out.
///
/// Reads the frame index at `+0x22C`, clears the whole `+0x210..+0x21C` group's
/// `+0xBB` "selected" bit, and then re-sets one or three of them depending on the
/// decremented index and the `+0x22B` byte.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_807be160` at `0x807BE160` (200 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/807be160_FUN_807be160.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - owner; four child pointers at `+0x210`/`+0x214`/`+0x218`/`+0x21C`,
///   arm byte `+0x22A`, qualifier byte `+0x22B`, frame index `+0x22C`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing; returns early when `+0x22A` is zero.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` and the four child pointers must be live; each child must have a
/// writable byte at `+0xBB`.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the early-out, the four clears, the `index - 1 == 8` test and the three
/// conditional sets are literal. The stored bit is bit 0 of each child's `+0xBB`
/// (`rlwinm ...,0,24,30` clears it, `ori ...,1` sets it).
