/// high - the two branches, the `cntlzw`-based `n == 1` gate (the `rlwinm ...,
/// 27,5,31` is `srwi 5`, so `clz >> 5 != 0` means "argument was 1"), the
/// `x < 10` / `y < 0x2A` bounds and the `v < 8` counter bump were all re-read
/// from the raw words. The two argument-less tail calls leave `r3` undefined in
/// the image, so they are modelled as `call0`.
