///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes `+0x7BC..+0x7F0` of all four records, calls `0x800B4710` per lane and
/// `0x806373C0` per lane, then `0x80637A40`, twelve `0x800C93D0` calls on
/// `+0x70`, `0x80637050`, `0x80637310`, `0x80637610`, three flag bytes and the
/// `+0x6A8` slot with `0x80826AE0`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be live, the `main.dol` pointer at `0x80429FB0` must be valid, and
/// `0x806373C0`/`0x80637A40`/`0x80637050`/`0x80637310`/`0x80637610` must be
/// valid functions.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the record offsets match the already-translated `fn_80637a40`
/// (`+0x00` byte, `+0x04..+0x24`, `+0x28..+0x2A` bytes, `+0x2C..+0x38` words).
/// Two export corrections from the raw words: (a) `0x80429FB0` is a *pointer*
/// that is dereferenced, and the `+0x48`/`+0x28`/`+0x08` words are read with a
/// four-byte lane stride from it while the `+0x58` byte is indexed by
/// `table[lane]` from `0x80354E60`; (b) the `+0x14` slot is written only when a
/// player exists, so it is deliberately not cleared in the zero branch.
