/// same `0x29C`/`0x22C`/`0x338C`/`0x16518`/`0x3394` offsets, the same
/// `0x800F57A0` gate, the same `0x800F56B0` + `0x800F9970` cursor walk and the
/// same `0x80C561E0` set/clear. The third argument of both walks is the incoming
/// `r4` (`mr r5,r28`, `mr r6,r28`), which is `course`, not the value Ghidra
/// mis-assigns to the `_savegpr` return. `0x802DCD5C`/`0x802DCDA8` are the
/// `_savegpr`/`_restgpr` helpers and are not emitted.
