/// `12.0` on Y; the result, minus the camera origin `+0xAC/+0xB0`, is written
/// to `+0x710/+0x714`. Pane `1` is used twice: its `(0, 20.0, 0)` offset vector
/// is rotated by the pane transform (`0x801C1160`) and averaged 50/50 with the
/// pane-5 position into `+0x708/+0x70C`, and after a fresh transform lookup its
/// translation is stored (plus `12.0` on Y) at `+0x700/+0x704`. Finally panes
/// `2..=5` are sampled relative to pane `1`, and the absolute X spread of each
/// is written to the four floats at `+0x718`.
