/// `lfs f0,0xE8(r3)` bit pattern, so the following `lfd f1,8(r1)` +
/// `fsubs f1,f1,f2` sees `x` and `176.0f`. `176.0f` is the single-precision
/// reading of the high word of the double at `0x807C_91C8`
/// (`0x43300000_80000000`), which is what `fsubs` consumes; the `li 2304` /
/// `xoris` low word (`0x00008900`) and the dead `lis r0,0x4330` never reach the
/// arithmetic. `fmuls f0,f0,f1`, `fctiwz`, the `lwz` low word, `neg r0,r0` and
