/// in `main.dol`. The loaded char is widened to a float through the compiler's
/// `2^52 + 2^31` double-magic sequence (`0x807C_98D0`), multiplied by the
/// single constant `48.0` at `0x807C_989C`, and subtracted from the float
/// pointed to by the second argument.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_806861e0` at `0x8068_61E0` (88 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel_d_basesNP/export/806861e0_FUN_806861e0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - object carrying the variant byte at `+0x348`.
/// * `out` - readable `f32` used as the base value.
///
/// # Returns
/// `*out - (table[variant] as i8 as f32) * 48.0`, rounded to single precision
/// (`fsubs`/`fmuls`).
///
/// # Side effects
/// None; both inputs are only read.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be live far enough to cover `+0x348`, `out` must be a readable
/// `f32`, and the `main.dol` table must be mapped.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the table base/index, the signed extension, the `0x43300000` magic
/// pair and the `48.0` multiplier are all explicit in the raw words. Ghidra
/// labels the return `double` only because of the `lfd` pair; the value is
/// produced by `fsubs f1,f0,f1`, so it is returned as `f32`.
pub unsafe fn fn_806861e0(this: usize, out: usize) -> f32 {
    let index = platform::read_u8(this + 0x348) as usize;
    let offset = platform::read_u8(0x8042_C1A0 + index) as i8 as f32;
    platform::read_f32(out) - offset * 48.0
}

