/// # Side effects
/// `0x8006DB30(+0x1EC)` feeds `0x800D9940(+0x2DC, probe, 0, 0)`; a non-zero
/// answer writes byte `1` to `+0x443` and ORs `0x8000` into `+0x274`. A
/// non-zero probe alone also writes byte `1` to `+0x443`.
///
/// # Safety
/// Both probe blocks must be initialised and `+0x443`/`+0x274` writable.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - same four-argument probe as the already translated `fn_80667d00`,
/// with the extra `+0x443` flag store; the independent `probe != 0` arm and the
/// `0x8000` mask are literal.
