/// Mirrors page/row into the `0x80429F7C` singleton (`+0x3E4`/`+0x3E8`) and,
/// when the page is `10`, stores the resolved pair into the `+0x770`/`+0x400`
/// table of that singleton, selected by bit `0x40` of `0x80429F80`. Finally
/// sets the `+0x50F` latch.
