/// Places `this` on the reference actor and re-derives its heading.
///
/// Called by [`fn_806cb210`] with the actor resolved from the `+0x40C` handle.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_806cb140` at `0x806CB140` (208 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/806cb140_FUN_806cb140.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - follower; angle `+0x104`, offsets `+0x53C`/`+0x540`, position
///   `+0xAC`/`+0xB0`.
/// * `other` - reference actor; angle `+0x104` (read as a signed halfword) and
///   position `+0xAC`/`+0xB0`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes `+0x104`, `+0xAC` and `+0xB0` of `this`.
///
/// # Safety
/// Both actors must be live.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the angle is `other.angle + 0x4000` stored as a halfword, the GQR3
/// `psq_l` reads it back as an unsigned 16-bit sample, the scale is
/// `0x807CB250` = 1/256, `0x80237C40` is the cosine helper and `0x80237BD0`
/// the sine helper; all four `fmuls`/`fadds`/`fsubs` operand registers were
/// checked against the raw words.
