/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_basesNP/export/8071eee0_FUN_8071eee0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - actor whose model holder is `+0x3B8`.
/// * `position` - address of three consecutive `f32` (`x`, `y`, `z`); the C
///   signature is `float *param_2` and it reads `param_2[0..3]`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// One virtual type test on the model, then one scene-adapter build and one
/// pane placement. No actor fields are read or written besides `+0x3B8`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `position` must address three readable floats and the model, if non-null,
/// must accept the `0x802F8FF0` tag on virtual `+0x08`.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the tag test, the null fallback, the `1` third argument and the
/// three float loads are literal; the roles of `0x8025C660`/`0x8025C470` and
/// `0x801C0C60`/`0x8023CFA0` are `// inferred:` from the same call shape in the
/// translated [`fn_806d9870`], and the overlapping C locals are reconstructed
/// as separate buffers (`adapter` is Ghidra's 68-byte `auStack_50`).
