/// Mode `2` stores the point and reports handle `2` with the caller's extra word
/// at `+0x71C`; mode `0` stores the same point and reports handle `6`; mode `1`
/// stores nothing but reports handle `7` with a zeroed object/`+0x71C`. Any other
/// mode is a no-op.
