/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80662e10` at `0x80662E10` (296 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80600000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel_d_basesNP/export/80662e10_FUN_80662e10.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - live ladder object; span `+0x3E8`, floor `+0x3E4`, four levels
///   `+0x3EC`, four player words `+0x408`, latch `+0x470`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes the four levels and `+0x470`, and calls `0x80052080` per live slot.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be live; the four `+0x408` words must be players or null.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - `count` is the main.dol word `0x80429CA0`, `0x807C8BE4`/`8B84`/`8BF0`
/// are `16.0`/`6.0`/`1.0`, and `0x807C8B88` is `2.4`. The prologue's
/// `_savegpr` at `0x802DCD6C` is the compiler helper named in the brief, so the
/// missing `this` argument comes back from `r3`.
